;;; `open` written as a guard's value loads, and a rule concludes a fact about
;;; it — regression `eq-value`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `r`'s guard `(eq ?y open)` binds `?y` to `open`, and `r` concludes `(q ?y)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is a name wherever the kernel does not read it, at the head of a
;;; written fact, a premise or a conclusion, and under an ordinary relation the
;;; head of a fact the kernel does not read (Q-M1f.66, Q-M1f.571): here it is
;;; written as a guard's value, so the program loads, and every command answers.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, root derives `(q open)`, and R is
;;; 16 states, exit 0 on every command.
;;; The engine loads it.
;;;

(relation a Thing :why "{?3} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?3} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?3} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(rule r ()
  :match  (and (a ?x) (eq ?y open))
  :assert (q ?y)
  :why "{?x} is an a, so {?y} is a q")
